    <body>
      <div type="work" n="64">
        <pb n="107"/>
        <head>64 — i — VI. — <quote>Because the mouth of liars shall be stopped</quote><ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a1" target="#n1" n="1"/>.</head>
        <div type="preface">
          <ab n="1">On <persName>Pilate</persName>'s Wife.</ab>
        </div>
        <div type="section">
          <ab n="2">By all methods, <persName>Christ</persName>, God, even in things that appear to be contemptible, thou <pb n="108"/> placedst a bit in the shameless mouth of the Jews. Accordingly <persName>Pilate</persName>'s wife, having even by means of visions and dreams been confirmed and brought to believe, openly sent a message to her husband, <quote>Have thou nothing to do [with that<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a2" target="#n2" n="2"/> just man; for I have suffered many things through<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a3" target="#n3" n="3"/> a dream to-day because of him<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a4" target="#n4" n="4"/></quote>; so that he also washed his hands with water in the sight of everyone, saying<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a5" target="#n5" n="5"/>, <quote>I am guiltless of the blood of this just man</quote><ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a6" target="#n6" n="6"/>. Then [the bloodthirsty wicked men drew<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a7" target="#n7" n="7"/> destruction upon themselves, saying, <quote>This man's blood be upon us all and upon our children</quote>; but thee they<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a8" target="#n8" n="8"/> showed forth as God, who art not the cause of evil things, and who wishest to [give life<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a9" target="#n9" n="9"/> to our race and not to destroy it as being merciful.</ab>
        </div>
      </div>
      <noteGrp>
        <note xml:id="n1" target="#a1" n="1"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 107, n. 7</orig></choice> Ps. lxiii, 12.</note>
        <note xml:id="n2" target="#a2" n="2"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 108, n. 1</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>before this</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n3" target="#a3" n="3"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 108, n. 2</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>in</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n4" target="#a4" n="4"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 108, n. 3</orig></choice> Matth. xxvii, 19.</note>
        <note xml:id="n5" target="#a5" n="5"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 108, n. 4</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>and said</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n6" target="#a6" n="6"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 108, n. 5</orig></choice> Ibid. 24, 25.</note>
        <note xml:id="n7" target="#a7" n="7"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 108, n. 6</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>also let the wicked men draw</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n8" target="#a8" n="8"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 108, n. 7</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>let them</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n9" target="#a9" n="9"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 108, n. 8</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>save</quote>.</note>
      </noteGrp>
